.TH XD\-FONTS 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-fonts \- the Fonts folder and font viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-fonts
.RI [ file ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without an argument,
.B xd\-fonts
is Windows XP's Fonts folder (Control Panel > Fonts): the fonts fontconfig
knows, as large icons, a list or details (Hide Variations shows each
family's regular face).
Opening one shows the font viewer, which prints a sample sheet.
Fonts installed from the folder are copied to the user's font folder;
fonts there can be deleted.
System fonts can't: they belong to the package manager.
.PP
With a
.IR file ,
it shows only the font viewer on that font file, as Windows' fontview
did.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/fonts/
The user's fonts (default
.IR ~/.local/share/fonts ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fc\-list (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
